From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nate Isern <nate@oxy.so>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Repack the Astro WebUI app into resources.pak

//chrome/browser/oxy/webui:resources builds astro_webui_resources.pak from the
Vite app, and astro_webui_page.cc serves every Astro surface out of the
resource map GRIT generates beside it. Neither of those puts the .pak inside
the browser. These two lines do, and until they exist the target produces a
.pak nothing loads and a resource map whose ids resolve to nothing at runtime
-- the page renders blank with no error, which is the exact failure that
condemned the previous, disk-served settings surface.

WHY A PATCH AND NOT THE OVERLAY

Both files are Chromium's. chrome/chrome_paks.gni is the repack list, and
tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec is the global id-space registry; an
overlay copy of either would be a whole-file overwrite of an upstream file
that churns every roll -- defect #7's shape exactly. Two hunks in a patch are
the reviewable form.

WHERE THE PAK ENTRY GOES

Inside `chrome_extra_paks`, in the `if (!is_android)` block whose own comment
reads "New paks should be added here by default." That template's output is
`resources.pak`, which is the bundle ui::ResourceBundle serves WebUI resources
from.

DECLARED LIMITATION: ANDROID IS NOT COVERED. The block is desktop-only, so an
Android build compiles the grit target (webui_controllers depends on it
unconditionally) and then repacks nothing, leaving the resource ids
unresolvable at runtime. Astro builds Linux today and the settings takeover in
060 lands in a desktop-only registration, so nothing regresses -- but an
Android build is not a supported configuration for the WebUI app until a
second entry exists in the Android branch, and this note is the only place
that says so.

WHY 2710, AND WHY NOT IN ALPHABETICAL ORDER

The integers in resource_ids.spec are fake start ids whose ORDER is the only
thing that matters; real ids are assigned from them plus the META sizes (see
tools/gritsettings/README.md). 2710 sits between about_sys at 2700 and
access_code_cast at 2720, which is that README's documented simple case: not
at a section boundary, and no `join` oddity nearby.

Strict alphabetical order would put chrome/browser/oxy ahead of
chrome/browser/resources -- that is, at the very head of the section, ahead of
about_sys, which is the entry carrying the section's `"align": 100` META. That
placement is the case the README tells you to avoid, and it would shift the
assigned ids of every entry after it for no gain.

The size bound is declared rather than counted because the .grd is generated:
the file list comes out of the app's manifest.json during the build and is not
readable from here. 500 against the 66 files the app emits today is roughly
seven times headroom, and exceeding it is a hard GRIT failure, not a silent
truncation.

Owned by https://github.com/OxyHQ/Astro/issues/14.
---
diff --git a/chrome/chrome_paks.gni b/chrome/chrome_paks.gni
--- a/chrome/chrome_paks.gni
+++ b/chrome/chrome_paks.gni
@@ -197,6 +197,7 @@ template("chrome_extra_paks") {
         "$root_gen_dir/chrome/access_code_cast_resources.pak",
         "$root_gen_dir/chrome/actor_overlay_resources.pak",
         "$root_gen_dir/chrome/app_service_internals_resources.pak",
+        "$root_gen_dir/chrome/astro_webui_resources.pak",
         "$root_gen_dir/chrome/autofill_ml_internals_resources.pak",
         "$root_gen_dir/chrome/bookmarks_resources.pak",
         "$root_gen_dir/chrome/browser/actor/resources/actor_browser_resources.pak",
@@ -252,6 +253,7 @@ template("chrome_extra_paks") {
       ]
       deps += [
         "//chrome/browser/actor/resources:browser_resources",
+        "//chrome/browser/oxy/webui:resources",
         "//chrome/browser/resources:dev_ui_paks",
         "//chrome/browser/resources/actor_overlay:resources",
         "//chrome/browser/resources/autofill_ml_internals:resources",
diff --git a/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec b/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec
--- a/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec
+++ b/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec
@@ -173,6 +173,21 @@
     "META": {"align": 100, "sizes": {"includes": [10]}},
     "includes": [2700],
   },
+  # Astro's WebUI app: every astro:// surface is one multi-entry Vite build,
+  # so one .grd holds the resources of all of them. Generated by
+  # //chrome/browser/oxy/webui:build_grd, hence the size bound — the file list
+  # comes out of the app's manifest.json at build time and is not parseable
+  # from here.
+  #
+  # Placed after about_sys rather than in strict alphabetical order (which
+  # would put chrome/browser/oxy before chrome/browser/resources, at the head
+  # of the section): about_sys carries this section's alignment META and is a
+  # split boundary, and reordering around it changes id assignment for every
+  # entry that follows for no gain.
+  "<(SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/chrome/browser/oxy/webui/astro_webui_resources.grd": {
+    "META": {"sizes": {"includes": [500]}},
+    "includes": [2710],
+  },
   "<(SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/chrome/browser/resources/access_code_cast/resources.grd": {
     "META": {"sizes": {"includes": [50]}},
     "includes": [2720],
